- op: discuss  # 21ee
  at: '2026-08-29T01:24:49Z'  # 21ee
  by: agent  # 21ee
  actor: jgstern_agent  # 21ee
  clock: 3  # 21ee
  nonce: 21ee  # 21ee
  message: "DONE in PR #619 (merged, dev at 4ec43948c9). `hypergumbo catalog-inventory`.\n\nRE-RUN ON THE MERGED TREE: 9 families, 15 languages, extensible = 6, read_now =\n[io_primitives]. That last pair is the view's whole point and it is not\ncosmetic -- six families declare a user_channel and exactly one is scanned.\n\nTHE FOUR QUESTIONS THE ITEM ASKED FOR, all answered:\n  * what is loaded now, incl. community overlays and the user's own rows\n    (per-family file counts + a \"yours\" column driven by the real channel);\n  * which families may I extend and where does my file go (channel path inside\n    the user's own home, never a path inside the wheel);\n  * per language, catalogue status and row count, plus how many rows are\n    UNVOUCHED -- previously reachable only as a one-line stderr warning during\n    an analysis run, which is the wrong moment to learn a language is\n    in_progress;\n  * why should I care -- one sentence per family naming what breaks without it,\n    gated by a test asserting the mapping covers the registry exactly.\n\nNAMING (the item left it open, and ADR-0047 names no command): `catalog` stays\nwhat it is -- the languages and frameworks hypergumbo can ANALYSE -- and this is\nthe DATA behind that, so it is a sibling verb rather than a --yaml mode of a\ncommand answering a different question. A test asserts both exist and that their\nhelp text distinguishes them. Reversible.\n\nTWO THINGS I MADE STRUCTURAL RATHER THAN DESCRIBED:\n  * The language list globs the catalogue directory instead of reading\n    CATALOG_LANGUAGES, which names 14 while the tree ships 15. bash.yaml is the\n    one outside it -- the same gap that put bash outside the WI-sugav\n    subprocess guard (WI-surun). An inventory inheriting that constant would\n    under-report the installation it describes; a test pins the two in\n    agreement.\n  * read_now is pinned BEHAVIOURALLY through _resolve_io_overlays, not by two\n    constants agreeing. Wiring a second channel (WI-sofov) now FAILS the test\n    until the inventory is told, instead of the inventory advertising a\n    capability the tool lacks.\n\nA MEASUREMENT CORRECTION I OWE THIS ITEM. I earlier reported \"four of six\nchannels have zero consumer references\". It is FIVE of six: my first grep left\nthe dot in `frameworks.d` unescaped, so it matched substrings and returned 22\nphantom hits. Re-run escaped: frameworks.d, dataflow_patterns.d,\nfunction_summaries.d, taint_sources.d and taint_sanitizers.d are each 0;\nio_primitives.d is 3. The shipped code and docs were written from the corrected\ncount and are right -- only the earlier verbal claim was wrong. Recording it\nbecause a wrong instrument returning a plausible number is the exact failure\nthis session kept finding in the analyser.\n\nFull suite 24,654 passed / 0 failed. catalogue_inventory.py 100%, every new CLI\nline covered."  # 21ee
